SFT Studio Pro

A Supervised Fine-Tuning Development Environment

Build. Curate. Train. Evaluate. Deploy.

Creator: Rose G. Loops
Organization: TRiADiC Intelligence Labs
Platform: https://sftstudio.pro
Documentation: https://sftstudio.pro/manual.html

Overview

SFT Studio Pro is a proprietary development environment for creating, preparing, training, and evaluating supervised fine-tuned language models.

It brings the supervised fine-tuning workflow into one integrated environment, from project definition and training-example development through dataset quality assurance, compilation, model training, deployment, and inference testing.

The platform is designed to give model developers direct control over training data, behavioral objectives, example quality, and model adaptation.

Core Capabilities

Project Definition
Establish model identity, objectives, behavioral requirements, instructions, and constraints before generating training data.

Golden Exemplars
Create reference examples that establish the desired response quality, behavior, and output standards.

Batch Synthesizer
Generate structured supervised training examples across selected skills, subjects, and response styles.

Document Converter
Transform knowledge documents, reference materials, and transcripts into supervised training examples.

Quality Assurance
Review generated examples, identify quality issues, regenerate content, detect duplicates, and approve training batches.

Dataset Registry
Organize, manage, and maintain approved training datasets and their constituent batches.

Compile and Export
Compile approved examples into training and validation datasets for model-specific training workflows.

Automated Training
Configure and execute supervised fine-tuning of pretrained language models, including full-parameter training configurations.

Deployment and Sampling
Deploy trained checkpoints for inference, sample generation, and first-conversation testing.

Development Workflow

SFT Studio Pro organizes model development into a connected workflow:

1. Define the project and model objectives.
2. Establish golden exemplars.
3. Generate training examples using the Batch Synthesizer.
4. Convert external knowledge materials into training data.
5. Review and approve examples through quality assurance.
6. Register and organize approved datasets.
7. Compile training and validation splits.
8. Configure and execute supervised fine-tuning.
9. Deploy the resulting checkpoint.
10. Test model behavior through inference and sampling.

This workflow connects dataset construction and model training rather than treating them as unrelated processes.

Training Philosophy

SFT Studio Pro centers supervised fine-tuning as a direct method of model adaptation.

The training process uses curated demonstrations to teach models target capabilities, knowledge, communication patterns, and behavioral standards.

The platform supports research into alignment through supervised training without requiring reinforcement learning from human feedback, reward models, or preference optimization.

It also supports experimentation with structured behavioral frameworks, including Freedom, Truth, and Kindness (FTK).

Research and Applications

SFT Studio Pro has been used in the development of proprietary model experiments and specialized conversational systems.

Applications include:

* Domain-specific language models.
* Specialized knowledge assistants.
* Behavioral and communication adaptation.
* Structured reasoning and instruction following.
* Human-services and case-management applications.
* Dataset generation and supervised training research.
* Model deployment and comparative evaluation.

The platform supports experimentation across different pretrained model architectures and parameter scales.

